  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a4ed5f55d63a8a14cb8fc3f6624472bf, type: 3}
  m_Name: firstCreate
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  key: firstCreate
  charName: Art, the Creativity Spren
  dialogue:
  - Fantastic! Most interactable objects in the museum will tell you how and when
    you can interact with them - but as a rule of thumb, press E to interact!
  - 'Now that you''ve collected your first archives grouping of archives, the next
    thing to knock off the checklist is to Restore your new works. '
  - As a curator at the Museum of Memory, you not only manage the museum - you create
    the works as well. While the right to each masterpiece must be collected via
    flashcard delivery, you have full reign to create any work you'd like to!
  - 'Here are a few quick pointers on creating your own masterpieces:'
  - 1. To expedite the curation process, you are given a limited amount of time to
    create each work - I recommend thinking of a masterpiece while looking at the
    full archive card, so you can make the most of your creation time!
  - 2. Archives at the Museum of Memory have a tendency to get mixed up - you'll
    spend a significant amount of time sorting through them. Make sure the works
    you create help you to remember the definition of each word - but there are no
    restrictions!
  - 3. After the initial creation of each masterwork, you can always touch them up
    later - don't feel pressured to get things perfect on the first try!
  - The Creation Station is now highlighted in yellow - go create some beautiful
    mnemonics!
  outlineTag: create
